// Title: File Deleted Via Sysinternals SDelete
// Sigma ID: 6ddab845-b1b8-49c2-bbf7-1a11967f64bc
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez (Cyb3rWard0g), OTR (Open Threat Research)
// Date: 2020-05-02 | Modified: 2023-02-15
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1070.004
// Description: Detects the deletion of files by the Sysinternals SDelete utility. It looks for the common name
//   pattern used to rename files.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage
// References:
//   - https://github.com/OTRF/detection-hackathon-apt29/issues/9
//   - https://github.com/OTRF/ThreatHunter-Playbook/blob/2d4257f630f4c9770f78d0c1df059f891ffc3fec/docs/evals/apt29/detections/4.B.4_83D62033-105A-4A02-8B75-DAB52D8D51EC.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_delete/file_delete_win_sysinternals_sdelete_file_deletion.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith ".AAA" or FolderPath endswith ".ZZZ") and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\Wireshark\\radius\\dictionary.alcatel-lucent.aaa"))
